load @/code/algebra/cayley-dickson
  find cayley-dickson-double

load @/code/algebra/normed-division
  find normed-division-algebra

note <The quaternions, the Cayley-Dickson double of the complex numbers, dimension four. A normed division algebra, still associative, but losing commutativity: the product of two quaternions depends on the order. This is the second loss of the tower. The unit quaternions of integer coordinates are the twenty-four points of the 24-cell, the binary tetrahedral group, which is why the directions of the substrate compose exactly and associatively.>

form quaternion
  link source, like cayley-dickson-double
  link algebra, like normed-division-algebra
